  "body": "> Replaces #334, which GitHub closed when its review fix was pushed after the fork left NeoTech's network. It includes that fix: `os_quit::request()` is `#[cfg(any(target_os = \"macos\", test))]`, so it is not dead code on Windows or Linux under clippy. The hands-on Cmd+Q check on macOS passed (see #334).\n\n## What changed\n\nOn macOS, Cmd+Q, the app menu's Quit, the Dock's Quit and a logout all send `terminate:` to NSApplication. winit 0.30.13's app delegate has no `applicationShouldTerminate:`, so AppKit ended the process at once. `CloseRequested` never arrived, and the unsaved-changes prompt (#107) was skipped. The menu also takes Cmd+Q before egui sees it, so the egui Cmd/Ctrl+Q shortcut never fired on macOS either.\n\n- New `crates/ui/src/egui_app/os_quit.rs`. On macOS, `install()` adds `applicationShouldTerminate:` to winit's delegate class through `class_addMethod`. The method answers `NSTerminateCancel` and only sets an atomic flag, so nothing can unwind across the FFI boundary. `class_addMethod` never replaces a method: if a future winit adds its own handler, the hook logs that and stays out. A missing AppKit, app or delegate is logged, never a panic. On other platforms `install()` does nothing.\n- `route_pending(state)` turns the flag into `actions::quit`, the same guarded Quit the window X sends. The shell calls it in `about_to_wait`, and un-minimises and focuses the window so the prompt is seen. A clean document quits through `el.exit()`, which does not go back through `terminate:`.\n- Dependency: `objc2 0.5`, the same binding and version winit already pulls in. It is macOS-only (`[target.'cfg(target_os = \"macos\")'.dependencies]`), and no new crate enters `Cargo.lock`.\n\nDecisions and the alternatives dropped are recorded in `docs/decisions/144-macos-cmd-q.md`: retargeting the menu item, replacing winit's default menu, and routing to `performClose:`.\n\nSide effect: cancelling the terminate also cancels a logout or shutdown while CamCraft is open, and macOS says CamCraft stopped it. That is the usual document-app behaviour. Letting the logout continue after the user answers was left out.\n\n## Readings\n\n- winit 0.30.13: `platform_impl/macos/menu.rs` wires Quit to `terminate:`, and `app_state.rs` implements only `applicationDidFinishLaunching:` and `applicationWillTerminate:`.\n- Live run on a Mac: a debug build with a clean document, sent `terminate:` via `NSRunningApplication.terminate`. The request went through the hook, and the app then exited with code 0.\n\n## Pinning test\n\n- `egui_app::tests::unsaved::os_quit_request_over_unsaved_changes_prompts_once`: an OS quit request over unsaved work is routed once, does not exit, and shows \"Unsaved changes\"; Don't Save then quits.\n\nGate: `scripts/gate.sh quick` ran as batch (Cargo files touched). Green apart from the known swarf_pose_continuity and the GPU-adapter headless tests (headless_run_succeeds, egui_headless_cli_exit_code_is_zero, headless_cli_exit_code_is_zero: no graphics adapter in this environment). clippy `-p camcraft-ui --all-targets -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Manual check (needs a Mac)\n\n1. `cargo run -p camcraft-ui`, then make the document dirty (the title gets `*`).\n2. Press Cmd+Q. The prompt should appear. Click Cancel: the app stays open.\n3. Choose app menu > Quit. The prompt should appear. Click Don't Save: the app quits.\n4. Make it dirty again and minimise. Right-click the Dock icon > Quit. The window should come back with the prompt.\n5. With a clean document, Cmd+Q quits at once.\n\nChangelog: macOS: Cmd+Q, the app menu's Quit and the Dock's Quit ask Save / Don't Save / Cancel over unsaved changes instead of quitting at once (#144)\n\nFixes #144\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
